===Etymology===
Likely from {{inh|en|enm|campion}}, a variant of {{m|enm|champioun}}; see {{m|en|champion}}. In classical times, the [[rose campion]] was fitted in garlands used to crown victors.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkæmpiən/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Some [[flowering plant]]s of the [[genus]] ''[[Lychnis]]''.
# Any flowering plant of the genus ''[[Silene]]''.
#* {{RQ:Hopkins Poems|poem=63|stanza=4|page=83|passage=Then over his turnèd temples—here— / Was a rose, or, failing that, / Rough-Robin or five-lipped '''campion''' clear / For a beauty-bow to his hat, {{...}}}}

